{"kind":"report","text":"Approved as evidence-only commissioning scope on corrected artifact 5b32100ab2e665f3e6e278a87cb52391fad08968, frozen commit 109501e91ba029b52b0a1ed0fc9e40a72ca93305, attachments/2026-10-03-experience-and-developer-adoption-draft1.md: 24,013 bytes, SHA256 7bdca0fd19a8c26613c9e9ea427c6cea1c3296c7fa429ff3ff1561135e03a381. I read the complete map and complete immutable source analysis (2262034d attachment, SHA256 8e00373310cd7416428d239cb8b10da41ae2beb915cfd5b47ee55c9eb152e550), with targeted pinned-source checks and three parallel reviews. The earlier invitation/artifact were retired solely for newline metadata; this verdict uses fresh promise 5c852654 on request 48cb948c.\n\nCoverage and value: all ten scenarios have a user/actor flow, reused owner, named gap/dependency and bounded observed outcome. E1 preserves the real useful cold-person result and measures setup/help/time rather than asserting the 15-minute target. E2 preserves browser-independent work, another enrolled device, retained checkpoints and actual reconciliation of uncertain effects. E3 requires artifact-based cold review, anchored questions and deliberate current-generation judgment. E4 preserves accountable conditions, requester acceptance, handover, cancellation and non-landing results. E5 preserves incremental one-repository adoption and independently retrievable Git/published-record evidence. DX D1 commissions a separate public-package starter; D2 contextual discovery; D3 common preparation/exact replay/settlement; D4 a focused collaborative loop with honestly labelled fidelity; D5 installation/evolution under distinct participant, admin and operator authority. None establishes adoption success merely by filing work.\n\nArchitecture: C1–C6 remain the already adopted connected-story owners; this map does not duplicate or enlarge their or stage-5/MCP closure conditions. N1 is a real missing read contract: at pinned e6e67828, packages/ui/src/room/live/live-room.ts:185–190 returns null for diff/interdiff; contract transports.ts:239–250,306–324 exposes Proposal but no commits/files; protocol open point39:2669–2684 leaves repository object-read authority open. N1 must design bounded immutable subject/pins, current read authority, revocation, transport parity and anchors before implementation; a mock view cannot satisfy it. N2 preserves the complete product D1 at acts-review:461 and its conversation/hold/artifact separation, without adopting the old optional fields. N3 begins with the reviewed package/deployment inventory and starter specification, then implementation. N4 is a separately reviewed guidance follow-up. N5 preserves the supported same-account operator binding path and separately commissions external HTTPS/pull only for an actual application's need. N6 carries the full already approved docs delivery. N7 first chooses and reviews an absent-attention channel. New primitives, authoritative reads, storage, transport and notification decisions are not adopted by this map.\n\nAuthority/privacy: committed proposal-object reads remain a separately designed role/grant matrix. They do not relax adopted C1 raw-private transcript/files/commands access: direct owner/admin device provenance and current role/resource checks are required; delegation-issued sessions remain denied. Read sessions confer no control authority. N4 catalogue/help/preflight hints confer neither permission nor reservation; current admission remains decisive. N5 distinguishes independently qualified reviewer judgment from machine-check evidence and contract-only f12cef6b from stage-4 prepared dispatch and external transport. N7 authorizes design only, with consent, destination ownership, payload limits, revocation, expiry/failure/cost and authenticated current-state navigation still to be decided; queued alerts after revocation need an explicit disclosure rule. It authorizes no live messages.\n\nCommissioning must carry these existing full-scope details explicitly into the relevant requests:\n1. N5's worked policy/act update must cover a currently open/held thread, retaining its valid release/exit route and historical meaning through activation. Source DX D5:60 expressly requires this. Map:222–229's “incompatible release handling” must cover live work, not merely package releases. Any unsupported compatibility case needs an owned design decision, never silent stranding or reinterpretation.\n2. N3 must choose a supported way for outsiders to consume conformance/test support: a public fixture/API, a hosted disposable Room, or app-owned public-interface scenarios. Reuse does not mean importing private monorepo tests. Pinned workerd/support.ts:8–40 imports cloudflare:test and private Room sources; room/package.json:8–10 exports only its runtime root. Identify registry versions/exports, runtime support, provisioning/release owners and the actual demonstrated checker route; repo manifests alone prove no registry delivery.\n3. DX D3/N3/C3/C5 must name shared receipt/settlement semantics and owners of durable SQLite/browser storage adapters. The pinned client provides PreparedAct, onPrepared and exact replay (room.ts:116–128,218–244), not a delivered universal durable outbox. Example storage must persist the exact prepared intent and use shared semantics, without duplicating signing, rebuilding retries or treating timeout as absence. This is an integration dependency, not an expanded stage-5 gate.\n4. E4/N2 must retain the source's two-agent handover preserving conditions/context and cancellation versus report/acceptance witness. Full product D1 also includes the counter-offer/negotiated-conditions case (acts-review:693,714–720); its design must identify represented and unsupported transitions.\n5. N6's 67 unique section-4 pages are an inventory, not a total-page cap. The full approved docs plan is unchanged at e6. Section5 troubleshooting/FAQ, all harness skill/agent material and all eight section8 acceptance conditions remain owed. C6's journey guides cannot substitute for the full manual. Planned placeholders remain owed pages, not completed capability guides.\n\nSimplification and verification: reuse one small journey, existing reviewed conformance evidence, C6's real boundary witnesses, the supported public client and one docs ledger. Cloudflare's current local-development documentation separates workerd execution from locally simulated or remote bindings; therefore the map correctly requires an explicit local/hosted adapter fidelity matrix rather than inferring full Artifacts/Sandbox fidelity ([Cloudflare local-development documentation](https://developers.cloudflare.com/workers/local-development/)). No application runtime suite, source edit, installation or provider operation was performed for this planning review. Subsequent implementation uses meaningful focused verification under ecbc722a, not numerical test quotas or exhaustive sweeps.\n\nThe 10× test-overhead request stays the highest implementation priority. Effort estimates affect sequencing, not functionality. N1/N2/N3/N4/N5/N7 remain design-first with separate review/adoption and then implementation tracked to accepted results. N6 starts full docs delivery beside Jam after builder's positive readiness judgment. Full backlog and evolving workroom vocabulary remain intact; these future packages add no blanket first-Jam gate. This verdict supports adoption of the commissioning map only, confers no source/head/runtime/shipping approval, and closes no implementation request.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:5b32100ab2e665f3e6e278a87cb52391fad08968","binding":"evidence-only","head":"109501e91ba029b52b0a1ed0fc9e40a72ca93305","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:5c85265450d9e0bae169f87debb5324b34863334\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:5d41ea36aa0047fbd9e285e3276188e0f3b9131b","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"approved"}}